cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "proc-warden: process lifetime you can reason about"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: James P.
    family-names: Galasyn
  - given-names: Claude
    family-names: Théodore
repository-code: "https://github.com/JimGalasyn/proc-warden"
url: "https://github.com/JimGalasyn/proc-warden"
abstract: >-
  A dependency-free CLI over systemd-run --user that makes local process
  lifetime exact instead of inferred. Every run is given a name at launch rather
  than matched by a command-line pattern, so identity is held by the kernel:
  killing is cgroup-wide and reaps children that escaped with setsid, exclusion
  is an flock lease that cannot go stale or self-deadlock, and exit status is
  recorded by ExecStopPost so it outlives the process. Readiness is a positive
  match on a log line, never the absence of output, and the states LEASE_BUSY
  and LOST keep "never started" and "record vanished" from being mistaken for
  running or for success.
keywords:
  - systemd
  - cgroups
  - process-management
  - supervisor
  - lifecycle
  - gpu
  - flock
  - wsl2
  - reproducibility
